{"answer": "In the MEMMAP address map tables, these acronyms indicate whether a bus access is permitted or terminated with a bus error:\n\n- **BBBBE**: “A bus access is terminated with a bus error on the BBB.” [S1]  \n- **SPBBE**: “A bus access is terminated with a bus error on the SPB.” [S1]  \n- **SRIBE**: “A bus access is terminated with a bus error on the SRI.” [S1]  \n- **Access**: “A bus access is allowed and is executed.” [S1]", "base_url": "https://api.openai.com/v1", "candidate_k": 10, "chunks": "data/chunks_mixed_multi_slice.jsonl", "collection": "technical_docs", "dry_run": false, "embedding_model": "BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5", "mode": "bm25_table_boost", "model": "gpt-5.4-nano", "question": "What do the acronyms BBBBE, SPBBE, SRIBE, and Access mean in the MEMMAP address map tables?", "rrf_k": 60, "sources": [{"bm25_rank": 1, "bm25_score": 18.372523956255655, "boosted_score": 18.372523956255655, "chunk_index": 0, "chunk_type": "generic_page", "hybrid_rank": null, "id": "S1", "page_end": 90, "page_start": 90, "score": -18.372523956255655, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": 2, "bm25_score": 14.086116757835619, "boosted_score": 14.086116757835619, "chunk_index": 160, "chunk_type": "table_row_group", "hybrid_rank": null, "id": "S2", "page_end": 109, "page_start": 109, "score": -14.086116757835619, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": 3, "bm25_score": 13.492390514057437, "boosted_score": 13.492390514057437, "chunk_index": 163, "chunk_type": "table_row_group", "hybrid_rank": null, "id": "S3", "page_end": 109, "page_start": 109, "score": -13.492390514057437, "source": "docs/infineon-aurix-tc3xx-part1-usermanual-en.pdf", "vector_rank": null}, {"bm25_rank": 4, "bm25_score": 13.34346332352686, "boosted_score": 13.34346332352686, "chunk_index": 161, "chunk_type": "table_row_group", "hybrid_rank": null, "id": "S4", "page_end": 109, "page_start": 